                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Old but gold.\r\n\r\nOn installing, I could not get 1080p or above to work with the cutscenes present, so I just used it as it came, and it ran smooth as butter with cutscenes but looked a bit ugly and jagged.\r\nHowever, if you can work out how to mess with it, I think you can get the modern scales and resolution sorted.\r\n\r\nThe game plays fun and arcadey, not too serious or realistic, for that matter. This is no way Ace Combat; you have a few missiles and your laser. Most fights are a dogfight and a few secondary weapons for each level.\r\n\r\nYou can command wingmen in the most basic way to attack, defend, etc. \r\nBasic, but they do achieve the goals you set.\r\n\r\nThere is an amazing variety of enemies, from fighters and tanks to massive dropships and buildings.\r\nThe levels are varied enough, with missions that all feel different even if you just shoot more stuff.\r\nOverall, for a few quid, this is well worth the money and time.\r\n\r\nLast thing I'd say is a MUST: read how to shake off when shot, as it really does make the game impossible to play with it; once gone, it's great and also takes a few seconds to take it off.",
